// Protocol between a Stampede server (the coordinator) and its workers.
//
// Workers dial out to the server and hold one bidirectional stream open,
// so they work from behind NAT and firewalls that only allow outbound
// connections. Everything the two sides say to each other travels on that
// stream as WorkerMessage and ServerMessage envelopes.
//
// Times are Unix nanoseconds. A time is in the clock of the side that
// produced it unless the field says otherwise; the server measures each
// worker's clock offset with ClockPing/ClockPong and converts.
